# No em dash

Never use the Unicode em dash (U+2014). Use the ASCII hyphen (-).

This applies to code, comments, documentation, commit messages, pull requests, UI and customer copy, tests, release notes, and generated prose.

Treat a newly introduced em dash as a style violation and replace it before committing.

Inbound supplier or customer text may still contain an em dash. Match that character with a Unicode escape (`\u2014` or `\x{2014}`), not a literal em dash in source.
